# VisionBot — ESP32-CAM AI-Thinker Pinout

## Camera (OV2640 — built-in, reserved)

| Signal | GPIO |
|--------|------|
| XCLK | 0 |
| SIOD (SDA) | 26 |
| SIOC (SCL) | 27 |
| VSYNC | 25 |
| HREF | 23 |
| PCLK | 22 |
| Y9–Y2 data | 35, 34, 39, 36, 21, 19, 18, 5 |
| PWDN | 32 |

> Do not use these pins for peripherals.

## VisionBot Peripherals

| Component | Signal | GPIO | Notes |
|-----------|--------|------|-------|
| Pan servo | PWM | 12 | Confirm in `pan_tilt_control.ino` |yellow or brown pin
| Tilt servo | PWM | 13 | Confirm in `pan_tilt_control.ino` |yellow or brown pin
| SSD1306 OLED | SDA | 14 | Confirm in `oled_status.ino` |
| SSD1306 OLED | SCL | 15 | Confirm in `oled_status.ino` |
| Onboard flash LED | — | 4 | Active HIGH |
| Onboard red LED | — | 33 | Active LOW |

## Power

| Rail | Source |
|------|--------|
| 5V in | USB or LiPo via regulator |
| 3.3V | Onboard LDO (500mA max) |
| Servo power | Separate 5V rail recommended |

> Servos draw transient current. Power them from a separate 5V rail.
> Do not power servos from the ESP32-CAM's 3.3V pin.

## Serial / Programming

| Signal | GPIO | Baud |
|--------|------|------|
| TX | 1 | 115200 |
| RX | 3 | 115200 |

Connect a USB-to-UART adapter (CH340 or CP2102).
Hold GPIO 0 LOW at boot to enter flash mode.
